### hilavitkutin-sym

Generic interned-identity core for the hilavitkutin ecosystem. `no_std`,
no alloc, no ecosystem dependencies. Provides `Sym`, a 4-byte
integer-equality handle whose 32 bits divide according to a `SymShape`
(three bits of domain tag by default), the `Domain` trait ladder that
distinguishes deduplicated-value domains from minted-fresh domains, the
`Interner` producer trait, and the `Generator` mint-only producer. A
minted handle is fresh within its generator and origin rather than
globally, and shapes with several origins make that disjointness
constructible. String interning is one domain of this core, supplied by
`hilavitkutin-str`.
